# Table of reactions for DEGAS-2

$Id$

# Reactions between particles to produce other particles.
# Each reaction is represented by four logical lines:
# (1) the full name of the reaction.  
# (2) the second is a blank-delimited sequence of entries of the form
# name particle + particle + ... -> particle + particle + ...
#
# When problemsetup is, run it will assume binary collisions with
# the first reagent being a background species and the second being a
# test species. Reactions between two background species are also
# permitted provided they yield test species; these reactions enter the
# problem as a source.
#
# With the "->" separating reagents and products, reactions are assumed to
# apply to all appropriate isotopically equivalent combinations. If the
# separator is "=>", the reaction will apply to only the species listed.
#
# (3) the file name with cross section data
# (4) the reaction classification

electron impact ionization of hydrogen
hionize	e + H *  -> e + H+ + e 
../data/hionize.nc
ionize_suppress

electron recombination of hydrogen 
hrecombine e + H+ -> H *
../data/hrecombine.nc
recombination

